
# ISR SOURCE MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED HERE.
# This repository is docs + release binaries only; the Rust tree is local-only
# and lives in ../ISR. A stale copy of it was found sitting untracked in this
# working directory (never committed), which one `git add -A` would have
# published. These entries make that impossible rather than relying on care.
/src/
/tests/
/e2e/
/target/
/Cargo.toml
/Cargo.lock
/build-artifacts/
/deployment-bundles/
/scripts/
/Dockerfile
/Makefile
/config.example.yaml

# Terraform provider CACHE written by running `terraform init` from this
# working directory — 643 MB of vendor binaries, none of it ours. The real
# module is 36 tracked files in ../ISR/terraform, include_str!'d into the
# binary (cloud.rs), so ISR emits it itself and this repo never needs it.
# Same class of accident as the /src/ entry above: one `git add -A` would
# try to publish it, and GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB anyway.
/terraform/
